;;; integral-laws.scm -- THE INTEGRAL OF A [0,+inf]-VALUED FUNCTION BY SIMPLE
;;; FUNCTIONS: the laws, proved from the definition, and the bricks they rest on.
;;; Agent M-2 of the October roadmap (week 2, scratchpad/triage/WEEK2.md;
;;; decision 4 of docs/roadmap-2026-10-03.md).  Helper prefixes ibk- (the
;;; bricks, sections A-E) and igl- (the integral, section F).  43 theorems,
;;; every one `modulo 0'.
;;;
;;; THE DEFINITIONS are structure-library/simple-integral.scm:
;;;   SIMPLE-INTEGRAL(omega, mu, s) = SUM_{y in s(omega)} y * mu({ s = y })
;;;   INTEGRAL(omega, cA, mu, f)    = ESUP { SIMPLE-INTEGRAL(s) : s simple, s <= f }
;;; (Rudin Def. 1.23).  INTEGRAL keeps the name and arity of the registered head
;;; integral.scm used to characterise by supports.
;;;
;;; THE SIX FORMER SUPPORTS OF integral.scm PROVEN HERE (same statements):
;;;   integral-in, integral-monotone, integral-sup-of-simple, integral-indicator,
;;;   integral-infinite-on-null, integral-homogeneous.
;;; NOT proven (left asserted for week 3, all resting on monotone convergence or
;;; on countable operations): integral-additive, integral-simple-approx,
;;; monotone-convergence, fatou, dominated-convergence, measurable-fn-eplus,
;;; measurable-fn-etimes, measurable-fn-sup, measurable-fn-liminf.
;;;
;;; THE ROUTE.  Everything about the simple integral is ONE lemma,
;;; `simple-integral-partition' (F3, the common refinement of Rudin Prop. 1.24 /
;;; the notes' Prop. 2.2): if s = hh o k with k : omega -> KS, KS finite, hh real
;;; and >= 0, and every fiber F_p = {k = p} measurable, then
;;;      SIMPLE-INTEGRAL(s) = SUM_{p in KS} hh(p) * mu(F_p).
;;; Monotonicity and additivity are its instances on the joint partition
;;; s(omega) x t(omega), k(x) = [s(x), t(x)] (igl-joint!); homogeneity on
;;; s(omega) itself; the indicator on {0} u {1}.  Then `integral-simple' (the
;;; supremum is attained at s: the integral of a simple function is its simple
;;; integral) makes integral-sup-of-simple the definition read back, and the
;;; others follow.
;;;
;;; SECTIONS.
;;;  (A) etimes algebra (extended-arith.scm defines etimes; nothing about its
;;;      algebra was proven): etimes-closed, -zero-left/-right, -one-left, -comm,
;;;      -distrib-left, -mono-left, -assoc-real, -distrib-right-real,
;;;      -mono-real-left.  The scalar is REAL where it matters (a simple function
;;;      has finite values).
;;;  (B) finite sums in a commutative monoid, pointwise-typed, by
;;;      finite-set-induction (ibk-induct!): finsum-cm-all-iden-ptwise,
;;;      -add-ptwise, -remove-ptwise, -fiber-ptwise (the comm-monoid twin of
;;;      finsum-fiber, which needs an abelian group), -pad-ptwise; the fiber
;;;      identities sep-fiber-insert-other / -same.
;;;  (C) finite sums in [0,+inf]: rps-finsum-le-ptwise (termwise comparison),
;;;      rps-finsum-scale-ptwise (a real scalar factored out).
;;;  (D) a measure on a finite partition, k^-1(K) as the disjoint union of the
;;;      fibers, by induction on K with no BIG-UNION:
;;;      sigma-algebra-preimage-finite-in, measure-preimage-finite-sum.
;;;  (E) level sets of a measurable function (IS-MEASURABLE-FN is the tail
;;;      criterion): measurable-fn-ge ({a <= f}, the archimedean property),
;;;      measurable-fn-level-set ({f = a}).
;;;  (F) the integral: the two unfold equations; integral-in, integral-monotone;
;;;      simple-integral-partition; simple-integral-in, simple-integral-mono,
;;;      integral-simple, integral-sup-of-simple; indicator-value-in/-out,
;;;      indicator-simple, simple-integral-indicator, integral-indicator;
;;;      integral-infinite-on-null; simple-integral-additive;
;;;      simple-integral-homogeneous; measurable-fn-finite-range,
;;;      simple-fn-scale; integral-homogeneous.
;;;
;;; LOAD WINDOW [3383, 3564) in load.scm LINE numbers.  lo: the latest
